 # Review findings
 
 - flapsim.py:9 `--selfcheck` was accepted mixed with other flags (e.g. `--selfcheck --seed 7` ran selfcheck), but spec/06 says it takes no other flags -> require `argv == ["--selfcheck"]` exactly, anything else falls through to normal parsing and exits on the unknown flag
-- flapsim.py:16 `int(argv[i + 1])` raised IndexError/ValueError tracebacks for a missing or non-integer flag value (also lines 18 and 20) -> bounds-check the index, validate with `lstrip("-").isdigit()`, and `sys.exit` with a message instead of crashing
+- flapsim.py:16 `int(argv[i + 1])` raised IndexError/ValueError tracebacks for a missing or non-integer flag value (also lines 18 and 20) -> wrap the parse loop in `try/except (IndexError, ValueError)` that exits with a message instead of crashing
 - flapsim.py:36 dead code: engine.run raises NotImplementedError when powerups=True (engine.py:11), so `st['shields']` is never returned and this branch can never execute -> remove the shields formatting until spec/07 is implemented
 - engine.py:9 signature added a positional `trace=None` beyond spec/00's documented `run(seed, ticks, flaps, powerups=False)` -> make it keyword-only (`*, trace=None`) so the documented positional surface is exact, and pass `trace=trace` at flapsim.py:35

